MID_EV12_034_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_034_m01_001: Baozi. In your heart of hearts, you know why you\nwere summoned.
MID_EV12_034_m01_002: I have a feeling you're going to tell me anyway. Is it\nbecause of my exemplary service to the Order?
MID_EV12_034_m01_003: In addition to your blunder with Majide, you also\nfailed us at Orion Canyon.
MID_EV12_034_m01_004: As one honored to be a member of the Guardians of\nthe Compass, you bring shame to our order.
MID_EV12_034_m01_005: Wouldn't you agree that these mistakes are grave?
MID_EV12_034_m01_006: I wasn't alone in this. Maria was with me, and don't\nyou forget it!
MID_EV12_034_m01_007: I've served the Order tirelessly, little boy. Don't try\nand shift the blame.
MID_EV12_034_m01_008: Comparing me to one of the Guardians of the\nCompass is like comparing a parent to a child.
MID_EV12_034_m01_009: Urk...
MID_EV12_034_m01_010: The old Ru Shou—your father, Lin Zhu—was a truly\nexceptional man.
MID_EV12_034_m01_011: After he died, we chose you to succeed him, and our\nexpectations for you were high.
MID_EV12_034_m01_012: But you've got to give me a chance!
MID_EV12_034_m01_013: You'll see—soon! I'm valuable to you, and the Order.\nI'll prove it!
MID_EV12_034_m01_014: Hm.
MID_EV12_034_m01_015: I will take you at your word. But listen to me, Baozi.
MID_EV12_034_m01_016: You have racked up a terrible debt. Your attitude,\nyour constant failures...
MID_EV12_034_m01_017: If you cannot correct these, then you will not only\nlose your position as a Guardian of the Compass.
MID_EV12_034_m01_018: You will be purged. I urge you to keep that in mind.\nNow, you may go.
MID_EV12_034_m01_019: Thank you, Magistra. Truly, thank you. I will meet\nyour expectations, mark my word.
MID_EV12_034_m01_020: Tch. They don't see me for what I really am—what\nI could be!
MID_EV12_034_m01_021: What a joke! Kill me? I won't let you!
MID_EV12_034_m01_022: Heh. Easy, Baozi. You have this. Just get them\nbefore they get you.
MID_EV12_034_m01_023: You watch, Magistra. I'll make you eat those\nwords. Soon.
MID_EV12_035_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_035_m01_001: Hm?
MID_EV12_035_m01_002: Yes. Regarding EX-477 and Tiamat, requesting\ndispatch of personnel to investigate.
MID_EV12_035_m01_003: Hm.
MID_EV12_035_m01_004: Who are you sending? Please repeat.
MID_EV12_035_m01_005: No, I have no objection to Myson. But as for\nCleobulus... There could be difficulties.
MID_EV12_035_m01_006: Very well. I have my doubts, but I will not further\nquestion your judgment.
MID_EV12_035_m01_007: As for the other matter... I will investigate and report\nback when I have learned more.
MID_EV12_035_m01_008: Ugh.
MID_EV12_035_m01_009: Well, there it is. Unreasonable requests that brook no\ndebate. Vritra is ever thus.
MID_EV12_035_m01_010: I had reached the conclusion you are not of the\nChurch of Seiros. True?
MID_EV12_035_m01_011: Indeed. The missionary Fabio, of the Church of\nSeiros, is a fabrication.
MID_EV12_035_m01_012: My true name is Anacharsis. I belong to a group\nknown as Agartha.
MID_EV12_035_m01_013: I have been entrusted with a mission. I am to\ninvestigate this land and report back.
MID_EV12_035_m01_014: This squares with what you said to the\nGrand Megalith.
MID_EV12_035_m01_015: So you do remember. In fact, that is precisely the\nmatter I was reporting in about.
MID_EV12_035_m01_016: Reporting to the entity that governs us, the serpent\nof chaos that engulfs the world—Vritra.
MID_EV12_035_m01_017: <NCA>Inquire about Vritra.
MID_EV12_035_m01_018: <NCB>Inquire about Kunlun.
MID_EV12_035_m01_019: <ACA>I cannot picture such a thing.
MID_EV12_035_m01_020: <ACA>Then I shall explain it in terms of Fódlan's culture.
MID_EV12_035_m01_021: <ACA>I am—and the Grand Megaliths were originally—\nruled by a god called Vritra.
MID_EV12_035_m01_022: <ACA>In this world, many organizations are ruled by gods,\nand mine, Agartha, is one such.
MID_EV12_035_m01_023: <ACA>These twinned authorities are the source of my\nmission. Vritra decides, and Agartha complies.
MID_EV12_035_m01_024: <ACB>There is another name I have heard: Kunlun. What\nof it?
MID_EV12_035_m01_025: <ACB>It is unknown even to us. You might think of it as a\nnew god, born in this land.
MID_EV12_035_m01_026: <ACB>The Grand Megaliths in Dagda have now joined the\nfold of Kunlun, a new god.
MID_EV12_035_m01_027: <ACB>And they now regard their former god, Vritra, and\nus, his adherents, as enemies.
MID_EV12_035_m01_028: <ACB>The latest information I have acquired has given me\nsome clues as to Kunlun's identity.
MID_EV12_035_m01_029: I had expected your explanation to be more\ncomplicated than this.
MID_EV12_035_m01_030: Cutting down a god—be it Vritra or Kunlun—is\nsomething I would relish.
MID_EV12_035_m01_031: You most certainly will not be able to "cut down"\nVritra, at any rate. He is unreachable.
MID_EV12_035_m01_032: For Vritra is there, or so they say.
MID_EV12_035_m01_033: Hmph.
MID_EV12_035_m01_034: The moon? I see. Even Answerer's blade could not\nreach so far...
MID_EV12_035_m01_035: Hmhmhm. I beg your pardon.
MID_EV12_035_m01_036: That reminds me, Dietrich, of something you may\nfind of interest.
MID_EV12_035_m01_037: During the Garland Moon in Fódlan, when you gaze\nupon the sky...you will see the Moon of the Rose.
MID_EV12_035_m01_038: It is beautiful.
MID_EV12_035_m01_039: Yes, it is.
MID_EV12_036_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_036_m01_001: Esteemed members of House Lamine! I have been\nlooking for you.
MID_EV12_036_m01_002: I am here today to bring you another Anna\nadministrative announcement!
MID_EV12_036_m01_003: That...fell flat. What's wrong?
MID_EV12_036_m01_004: On with it.
MID_EV12_036_m01_005: Tough crowd... Ahem.
MID_EV12_036_m01_006: The particulars of your next match have been\ndecided, so I am here to kindly inform you!
MID_EV12_036_m01_007: They're written down in brief here, so take a\ngood look!
MID_EV12_036_m01_008: <TLP>House Lamine\n\nMatch: Third Qualifier of the Heroic Games\nOpponent: Twin Jewels of Arago\nLeaders: Nathan, Creek\n\nDate: {DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}
MID_EV12_036_m01_009: Before you go... Just one question's eating at me.
MID_EV12_036_m01_010: These Twin Jewels of Arago... I can only think of one\npair that goes by that name.
MID_EV12_036_m01_011: Yeah, you got it! They're Aragonian heroes, and\nthe pride of their kingdom.
MID_EV12_036_m01_012: Nathan the Red, known as the Catoblepas. And\nCreek the Green, the Pantere.
MID_EV12_036_m01_013: <NCA>Express interest.
MID_EV12_036_m01_014: <NCB>Let it lie.
MID_EV12_036_m01_015: <ACA>Are these men as strong as their reputation?
MID_EV12_036_m01_016: <ACA>They're absolute monsters. I've heard the two of\nthem took on a horde of three hundred bandits.
MID_EV12_036_m01_017: <ACA>That's not all. In Arago, they made their name by\nbattling giants.
MID_EV12_036_m01_018: <ACA>There's no end of the tales about these two. Just\nwalk into a tavern in Arago and ask.
MID_EV12_036_m01_019: <ACA>As soon as the conversation turns to the kingdom's\nstrongest, you're sure to hear of the Twin Jewels.
MID_EV12_036_m01_020: <ACA>They just might eclipse the strength of the\nWhite-Maned Demon.
MID_EV12_036_m01_021: <ACA>Really? I mean, even in a tiny fishing village like\nFina, we'd heard of them. But is all this true?
MID_EV12_036_m01_022: <ACA>Dagda is huge...and packed with strong people,\napparently. They just keep turning up!
MID_EV12_036_m01_023: Given their fame, I find it peculiar that we had yet\nto hear of their participation in the games.
MID_EV12_036_m01_024: Well... Truth is, it was only just pushed through.
MID_EV12_036_m01_025: So they were allowed to join partway? Like us!
MID_EV12_036_m01_026: Rumor has it that someone who favors Arago pulled\nsome strings.
MID_EV12_036_m01_027: I'm not privy to the exact details, but the\ncommissioner of the games has a lot of latitude.
MID_EV12_036_m01_028: A tardy admission at the will of the state? I wonder\nwhat machinations drive this.
MID_EV12_036_m01_029: That is of no concern to me. I welcome any and all\nwho are strong.
MID_EV12_037_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_037_m01_003: Ohoho... The tension sure is thick in here.
MID_EV12_037_m01_004: You must be our allies for the round. Give our rivals\nhell out there, and I promise to do the very same.
MID_EV12_037_m01_005: I can't afford to lose here either, you see.
MID_EV12_037_m01_007: Welcome news. But forgive me, you are...?
MID_EV12_037_m01_008: Right, I haven't introduced myself. Talimun, chief\nexecutive of the Vandahl Trading Company.
MID_EV12_037_m01_009: Vandahl Trading Company... Like the one down by\nthe port?
MID_EV12_037_m01_010: That's the one. I'm head of the company. You may\nnot believe it, but I'm the richest man in Dagda.
MID_EV12_037_m01_011: Hee hee. It sounds like money is your whole\nworld, isn't it, Talimun?
MID_EV12_037_m01_006: My name is Orchel. Let's all go out there and give\nthis battle our very best!
MID_EV12_037_m01_012: {SetColor=Gray}Hm. I'm getting a reaction like that girl has one\nof Drake's treasures, but...that can't be right.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_037_m01_013: {SetColor=Gray}If the compass says she's got one, then she does, but\neveryone who carries them has one thing in common.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_037_m01_014: {SetColor=Gray}They all have daggers behind their eyes. But there\nisn't any hint of that with her.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_037_m01_015: {SetColor=Gray}Wait—another one? Who is it now?{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_037_m01_016: *sigh*
MID_EV12_037_m01_017: Now this guy...there's a dagger behind everything\nabout him. I may cut myself just looking at him.
MID_EV12_037_m01_042: Ah. So it's him, is it? And as always, there's more\nthan just daggers behind those eyes.
MID_EV12_037_m01_018: Must I feel your glare?
MID_EV12_037_m01_019: Ah! Forgive me. It's just—you have such a pretty\nface, I couldn't help but get lost in your eyes.
MID_EV12_037_m01_020: To think there are still people like him out there in\nthe wide world... Best to let it be for now though.
MID_EV12_037_m01_021: That—that's one of Fódlan's Heroes' Relics! Is this\nman a descendant of one of the 10 Elites?!
MID_EV12_037_m01_001: So it's you. I should tell you that, during today's\nbattle, I will have my eyes trained on you.
MID_EV12_037_m01_002: As you wish. And if it pleases you, cut me down.
MID_EV12_037_m01_040: So it's you. I should tell you that, during today's\nbattle, I will have my eyes trained on you.
MID_EV12_037_m01_041: As you wish. And if it pleases you, cut me down.
MID_EV12_037_m01_022: That mask... Do you like cats?
MID_EV12_037_m01_023: I do! A lot. Though they do tend to run from me...
MID_EV12_037_m01_024: My sister likes cats. They run from me as well.
MID_EV12_037_m01_025: She believes it is because my blood lust is too strong.
MID_EV12_037_m01_026: Oh, you have a sister? I'm sure she's a perfect lady.
MID_EV12_037_m01_027: You are correct. Her name is Elfrida. She is beautiful.
MID_EV12_037_m01_028: {SetColor=Gray}What's this? Sweetie not just talking to someone, but\nabout his family?{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_037_m01_029: *gasp* Is it because she likes cats? Wait! Sweetie\nlikes cats! What a turn of events...
MID_EV12_037_m01_030: Oh, that's so cute! If only I was a cat... What would\nit be like though? Meow.
MID_EV12_037_m01_031: Take your daydreams elsewhere! This is a battle, not\nthe land of make-believe.
MID_EV12_037_m01_032: A girl has to have her fantasies. Let me dream!
MID_EV12_037_m01_035: {SetColor=Gray}What's this? Sweetie not just talking to someone, but\nabout his family?{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_037_m01_036: *gasp* Is it because she likes cats? Wait! Sweetie\nlikes cats! What a turn of events...
MID_EV12_037_m01_037: Oh, that's so cute! If only I was a cat... What would\nit be like though? Meow.
MID_EV12_037_m01_038: Take your daydreams elsewhere! This is a battle, not\nthe land of make-believe.
MID_EV12_037_m01_039: A girl has to have her fantasies. Let me dream!
MID_EV12_037_m01_033: Enough chitchat. It seems the match is already\nabout to begin.
MID_EV12_037_m01_034: Time to grade these Twin Jewels. We'll see how\nthey hold up under the light.
MID_EV12_066_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_066_m01_001: The Cleansing of Damascar—the most lamentable\nevent in our illustrious history.
MID_EV12_066_m01_002: The accursed Damascar, whose children were\ndelivered from death by the mercy of Yu Phas.
MID_EV12_066_m01_003: The country's history has been all but lost, and all\nthat remains are mysteries. Can you picture it?
MID_EV12_066_m01_004: Journey with me back to a time when prosperous\nDamascar rebelled against Dagda the Great.
MID_EV12_066_m01_005: Incensed, he dispatched his general Caius and a\nforce of men one hundred thousand strong.
MID_EV12_066_m01_006: He ordered that the accursed kingdom, Damascar,\nbe erased from the Dagdan Empire!
MID_EV12_066_m01_007: In the Eastern Division, the Twin Jewels of Arago,\nrenowned for bravery, will fight as the Dagdan army!
MID_EV12_066_m01_008: In the Western Division, our ragtag heroes take the\nrole of Damascar's hordes!
MID_EV12_066_m01_009: Quiver with anticipation, onlookers, for our epic\nbattle is about to begin!
MID_EV12_066_m01_010: The kingdom of Damascar... Diego, isn't that your\nancestral land?
MID_EV12_066_m01_011: It was the homeland of the Har Hali and all\nforest peoples.
MID_EV12_066_m01_012: That place was destroyed hundreds of years ago.\nStill, none of that matters to me anymore.
MID_EV12_066_m01_013: Not much, anyway. But I'm glad we're in the\nWestern Division. I'd hate to be on the other side.
MID_EV12_066_m01_014: Even when we have to leave home, Diego, our\nhomeland is always part of our heart.
MID_EV12_066_m01_015: A mask of deiform gold. So this is the priest the\nchancellor is fixated on.
MID_EV12_066_m01_016: Look at the craftsmanship! That mask won't easily\nbe broken.
MID_EV12_066_m01_017: Excuse me... Why are you staring so intently\nat my face?
MID_EV12_066_m01_018: Forgive my rudeness. I find myself interested in\nyour mask.
MID_EV12_066_m01_019: I hear that a lot! I'm quite fond of it myself.
MID_EV12_066_m01_020: A voice fairer than I'd imagined. Now I'm getting\ncurious about what's under the mask...
MID_EV12_066_m01_021: So you're the Twin Jewels of Arago. What a lovely\npair the two of you make.
MID_EV12_066_m01_022: I've heard there have been riots ever since the new\nking's ascension. Your reputation precedes you.
MID_EV12_066_m01_023: Baseless rumor, you can be sure. Ignore him, Nathan.
MID_EV12_066_m01_024: Your delight in ruthless oppression has created\nquite the powder keg at home, hasn't it?
MID_EV12_066_m01_025: Rrgh...
MID_EV12_066_m01_026: Pay him no mind! It's all a gambit. He cares for\nnothing but winning this battle.
MID_EV12_066_m01_027: I scent strength—from both of you.
MID_EV12_066_m01_028: I hope today will indeed be a pleasurable one. I ask\nonly that you try.
MID_EV12_066_m01_029: I can't deny that you've won up till now, but you're\nan odd bunch.
MID_EV12_066_m01_030: Keep your wits about you, Creek. We can't fail.
MID_EV12_066_m01_031: We're representing the kingdom, after all. Losing\nface is not an option.
MID_EV12_038_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_038_m01_001: Excellent work out there, everyone... Wait—where'd\nthat pretty girl go?
MID_EV12_038_m01_002: No pretty girls here, just me!
MID_EV12_038_m01_003: I know you mean the priest. She's not feeling well, so\nshe left.
MID_EV12_038_m01_030: No pretty girls here, just me!
MID_EV12_038_m01_031: I know you mean the priest. She's not feeling well, so\nshe left.
MID_EV12_038_m01_004: I was hoping to ask her a question or two... Ah well.\nMaybe next time.
MID_EV12_038_m01_005: More importantly, then... Dietrich, let's talk business.
MID_EV12_038_m01_006: I'll get to the point. That grotesque sword of yours...\nWould you be willing to sell it?
MID_EV12_038_m01_007: Lay hands on this blade? You do not understand\nwhat it is, do you? You would regret it, I assure you.
MID_EV12_038_m01_008: That's one of the legendary weapons of Fódlan—one\nof the Heroes' Relics, is it not?
MID_EV12_038_m01_009: Well, well. You are impressively knowledgeable for\na Dagdan.
MID_EV12_038_m01_010: I have business in Fódlan too. I hear all sorts of\nstories in my travels, you see.
MID_EV12_038_m01_011: It is the fell blade Answerer, passed down in my\nhouse. As you say, it is a Hero's Relic.
MID_EV12_038_m01_012: I've heard it's forbidden to remove a Hero's Relic\nfrom its house.
MID_EV12_038_m01_013: I never imagined I'd be seeing one here in Dagda.\nIt's exhilarating.
MID_EV12_038_m01_014: Ursula, with all that in mind, how much gold can\nwe afford to spend on this beauty at the moment?
MID_EV12_038_m01_015: In light of the ongoing tax situation, wages owed,\ncost of the Zaratan's repairs, and everything else...
MID_EV12_038_m01_016: I believe the company can afford an expenditure\nof the appropriate amount without issue.
MID_EV12_038_m01_017: Alright then. Dietrich, I'll give you 3.9 million gold\nfor that sword.
MID_EV12_038_m01_018: Talimun! I said an appropriate amount! That offer\nis easily triple what's reasonable. It's too reckless.
MID_EV12_038_m01_019: It's an offer from the heart! He's not the type to be\nmoved by anything but drastic actions.
MID_EV12_038_m01_020: Don't worry, Ursula. Something tells me that sword\nis worth every piece of gold I'm offering.
MID_EV12_038_m01_021: That number's so big I can't make sense of it. What\ncould you do with that much money?
MID_EV12_038_m01_022: Were you so inclined, you could build a castle—a\nlarge one.
MID_EV12_038_m01_023: That... That is crazy. How much money do\nyou HAVE?
MID_EV12_038_m01_032: That number's so big I can't make sense of it. What\ncould you do with that much money?
MID_EV12_038_m01_033: Were you so inclined, you could build a castle—a\nlarge one.
MID_EV12_038_m01_034: That... That is crazy. How much money do\nyou HAVE?
MID_EV12_038_m01_024: The most. And now that I've demonstrated my\nsincerity, what do you say, hm?
MID_EV12_038_m01_025: I have no choice but to reject it. Only death could\npry this blade from my hand.
MID_EV12_038_m01_026: I had a feeling you'd say something like that. What,\nno use for money? Or is it just the sword?
MID_EV12_038_m01_027: How about that cloak, hm? I can make you a nice\noffer on that.
MID_EV12_038_m01_028: Ink-Black Wen? No way! Sweetie's the only one who\ncan wear it.
MID_EV12_038_m01_029: Alright, alright... Well, if you're ever short on cash,\njust bring it by Vandahl Trading.
MID_EV12_039_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_039_m01_001: What is the meaning of this?
MID_EV12_039_m01_002: Our sister has been reborn? Into a new\nmechanical body?
MID_EV12_039_m01_003: Difficult to credit, but Credna has the ability to do it.
MID_EV12_039_m01_004: At least this offers us an explanation for some truly\ninexplicable things.
MID_EV12_039_m01_005: Like how a mere machine exhibits power over\nFather's remains and control over the risen dead...
MID_EV12_039_m01_006: No. That girl is not Yu Phas. She cannot be.
MID_EV12_039_m01_007: We saw Yu Phas fall into Dagda's cauldron and die.
MID_EV12_039_m01_008: Since that day, her soul has been stored in a phial\nas flamma.
MID_EV12_039_m01_009: Tch...
MID_EV12_039_m01_010: Father's soul clamors... It burns!
MID_EV12_039_m01_011: It seems even Father senses his daughter... How\ncould he not?
MID_EV12_039_m01_012: Please, Father. Still your heart!
MID_EV12_039_m01_013: Turns out that stone the magistra clings to is more\nthan just a trinket.
MID_EV12_039_m01_014: I thought Gleipnir was something, but this, well...
MID_EV12_039_m01_015: I've had enough of these harpies.
MID_EV12_039_m01_016: I think I'll take that stone as a going-away present...\nto myself.
MID_EV12_039_m01_017: If it's got power, I can use it. If not, I can sell it.
MID_EV12_039_m01_018: Damn, though. Never would have figured that the\nmagistra is a looker under that mask.
MID_EV12_039_m01_019: That's one body I'd love to ensnare... You had me\nfooled! But not anymore.